@startuml pigeonhole-principle
' D8 — Pigeonhole principle behind WallBreaker's split.
' Depicts: <=k unit edits over k+1 contiguous pieces leave >=1 piece undamaged, an
' exact substring seed; transposition / merge-split need 2k+1 (boundary-spanning edit).
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName "DejaVu Sans"
skinparam rectangle {
  BorderColor #34495E
  FontName "DejaVu Sans"
}
title Pigeonhole principle behind WallBreaker's split\n<latex>\le k</latex> unit edits over <latex>k+1</latex> contiguous pieces  ⇒  <latex>\ge 1</latex> undamaged piece

rectangle "query q split into <latex>k+1 = 3</latex> contiguous pieces   (k = 2)" as HDR #FDEBD0

rectangle "piece 1\n✗ an edit lands here" as P1 #FADBD8
rectangle "piece 2\n✗ an edit lands here" as P2 #FADBD8
rectangle "piece 3\n✓ undamaged" as P3 #D5F5E3
HDR -[hidden]down- P1
P1 -[#E74C3C]-> P2
P2 -[#AAB7B8]-> P3

rectangle "at most k = 2 pieces can be damaged\n(each unit edit dirties ≤ 1 piece)" as MID #EAECEE
rectangle "piece 3 is an EXACT substring of the target term\n⇒ seed the SCDAWG lookup here" as SEED #D5F5E3

P1 -[hidden]down- MID
P3 -[#2ECC71]-> SEED : undamaged

note bottom
  With <latex>\le k</latex> substitutions / insertions / deletions spread over <latex>k+1</latex> pieces,
  the pigeonhole principle forces at least one piece to escape every edit — an exact
  substring seed for the dictionary search. Transposition and Merge/Split need
  <latex>2k+1</latex> pieces: one boundary-spanning edit can corrupt two adjacent pieces at
  once, so k such edits may dirty up to 2k pieces. (Counts are Coq-verified upstream.)
end note
@enduml
